  "Visual_Landing": "Add Dimensions (at least 2) and a Measure to build the dynamic matrix. Optional: an ID in Detail (rows) makes averages and distinct counts exact. Pro plan on Microsoft AppSource: up to 10 dimensions and 5 measures, distinct counts, percentage values, totals and row groups.",
  "Visual_Layout": "Layout",
  "Visual_MaxColor": "Maximum value color",
  "Visual_MaxCols": "Maximum columns",
  "Visual_MaxRows": "Maximum rows",
  "Visual_Measures": "Measures",
  "Visual_MidColor": "Middle value color",
  "Visual_MinColor": "Minimum value color",
  "Visual_Msg_AddDimension": "Add at least one dimension.",
  "Visual_Msg_AddMeasure": "Add at least one measure.",
  "Visual_Msg_SelectXY": "Select X and Y to begin.",
  "Visual_Msg_TwoDimensions": "You need at least 2 dimensions to generate the matrix.",
  "Visual_Notice_AvgOfAvg": "This is an average of averages. Power BI averaged the field at the grain of every bound dimension, and those averages are combined here, so each combination counts the same whether it holds one row or ten thousand. The weights are not in the data the visual receives, so it cannot correct for them. Add an ID to Detail (rows) — the order, ticket or customer — and the visual computes the exact average.",
  "Visual_Notice_Hidden": "{dim}: {n} of {total} values left out, and out of the totals.",
  "Visual_Notice_NonAdditive": "This measure is being collapsed in the visual: Power BI aggregated it at the grain of every bound dimension, and the rest is combined here. If the measure is not additive — a distinct count, a ratio, a percentage — the number may not be the one you expect. For a distinct count, put that column in Dimensions or Detail (rows) and it is counted exactly; otherwise bind only the dimensions you compare, or use an additive measure.",
  "Visual_Notice_Others": "{dim}: {n} of {total} values grouped as Others.",
  "Visual_Notice_Partial": "Showing a partial dataset — the row limit was reached. Reduce the number of dimensions for exact values.",
  "Visual_Others": "Group the rest as Others",
